# Crafted ELPA width-1 tail block corner: 13 H x 5 spherical basis functions
# = nao 65 = nbw + 1 (nbw = 64). With an unfixed ELPA (cp2k#3297, cp2k#4484) the
# serial tridiag_band flush underflows its Householder-vector slot accounting for
# such matrix orders and smashes the heap - this crashes already at one rank, at
# the very first diagonalization. At two ranks this input passes with unfixed
# ELPA as well; the np2 deadlock corner of the same bug family is covered by
# tailblock_hang.inp. Single SCF step: the matcher checks the energy of the one
# ELPA diagonalization, no iterative amplification of rounding differences.
&GLOBAL
  PREFERRED_DIAG_LIBRARY ELPA
  PRINT_LEVEL LOW
  PROJECT H13-tailblock
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
&END GLOBAL

&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    BASIS_SET_FILE_NAME BASIS_MOLOPT
    CHARGE +1
    POTENTIAL_FILE_NAME POTENTIAL
    &SCF
      IGNORE_CONVERGENCE_FAILURE
      MAX_SCF 1
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PBE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      A 10.0 0.0 0.0
      B 0.0 10.0 0.0
      C 0.0 0.0 10.0
      PERIODIC NONE
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      H 5.000000 5.000000 5.000000
      H 3.797448 6.155648 5.271473
      H 4.777392 6.674116 4.925509
      H 5.228785 4.196111 3.374263
      H 4.758039 4.665234 3.561049
      H 4.076643 5.192930 3.709559
      H 5.995970 5.617533 6.225215
      H 3.715393 2.529142 6.241812
      H 2.222153 4.617737 5.793007
      H 6.913129 6.921863 5.929592
      H 7.097115 6.833777 6.042256
      H 7.459249 4.014086 6.132501
      H 5.598309 2.987267 6.867141
    &END COORD
    &KIND H
      BASIS_SET DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH-q1
      POTENTIAL GTH-PBE
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
